  "rationale": "The budget (200/200 evals) and round cap (2/4) are exhausted, forcing a stop. The current Pareto front is robust and feasible: the minimum area design (pipelined_m, 1554 LUTs+FFs) meets all constraints with 14.3 bits of accuracy (max_abs_err 5.02e-05 < 2.44e-04) and a system batch latency of 0.167 us (well under the 0.44 us limit). The front spans a wide trade-off space (1554 to 3610 LUTs+FFs, 14.3 to 18.4 bits accuracy) and covers the hypervolume reference point (4000, 12) comfortably. The selection rule (min luts_plus_ffs) will pick the 1554 design, which has significant margin on both accuracy and system latency constraints."
